{"id": 3484, "name": "Twelve Foot Falls County Park", "read": "2026-10-15", "pages": [{"url": "https://www.marinettecountywi.gov/parks/camping/twelve_foot_falls_park_campground/", "lines": ["| | | | | | | | | Campgrounds » Twelve Foot Falls Park Campground | | | | ATV/UTV Usage in Marinette County Parks - More Details | | | Credit Card Fee | There is a 2.5% convenience fee for all credit card transactions. ($2.00 minimum) | | | Twelve Foot Falls Park Campground Find A Campsite | | | | Interactive Map | | | | | | | | | | Twelve Foot Falls Campground has twelve (12) non-electric campsites. Five (5) campsit", "ue waterfalls, hiking trails, trout fishing, vault toilets and a hand pump to access potable water. Reservations available 184 days in advance. | | Marinette County Visitor Guides & Waterfall Map | | Fees: Rustic Sites: $20.00/ night per site Reservation Fee: $10.00/site non-refundable Firewood: No firewood available in the park. Wood can be purchased at various businesses in Pembine or at Twin Bridge Park or Morgan ", "Firewood: No firewood available in the park. Wood can be purchased at various businesses in Pembine or at Twin Bridge Park or Morgan Park between 3:30 - 4:00 p.m. Dump Station: Located at Twin Bridge Park 5 Miles South ($20.00 fee for non-registered campers) Day Use Fee Only: $5/day at entrance or with an annual Marinette County sticker Opens: May 1 | Closes: Oct 15 | | | | Check-In Time: 3:00 pm | Check-Out Time: 12", "e held for the length of the reservation unless the Parks Office is notified of the cancellation. Failure to notify the Parks Office during reservation hours, will result in loss of all camping and reservation fees. The $10.00 reservation fee is non-refundable. Refund of camping fees are given in the form of a voucher and may be used towards a reservation at any Marinette County Park anytime during the remainder of t", "ions: Four or more days notice: If the cancellation request is received in the parks office four (4) or more days